ry=KCC4&submit=Search", "KCC4")	=HYPERLINK("http://db.yeastgenome.org/cgi-bin/search/quickSearch.pl?query=PRX1&submit=Search", "PRX1")	=HYPERLINK("http://db.yeastgenome.org/cgi-bin/search/quickSearch.pl?query=FLC2&submit=Search", "FLC2")	=HYPERLINK("http://db.yeastgenome.org/cgi-bin/search/quickSearch.pl?query=HSC82&submit=Search", "HSC82")	=HYPERLINK("http://db.yeastgenome.org/cgi-bin/search/quickSearch.pl?query=DDR2&submit=Search", "DDR2")	=HYPERLINK("http://db.yeastgenome.org/cgi-bin/search/quickSearch.pl?query=SUB1&submit=Search", "SUB1")	=HYPERLINK("http://db.yeastgenome.org/cgi-bin/search/quickSearch.pl?query=SFC1&submit=Search", "SFC1")	=HYPERLINK("http://db.yeastgenome.org/cgi-bin/search/quickSearch.pl?query=SNF2&submit=Search", "SNF2")	=HYPERLINK("http://db.yeastgenome.org/cgi-bin/search/quickSearch.pl?query=YET2&submit=Search", "YET2")	=HYPERLINK("http://db.yeastgenome.org/cgi-bin/search/quickSearch.pl?query=FRA1&submit=Search", "FRA1")	=HYPERLINK("http://db.yeastgenome.org/cgi-bin/search/quickSearch.pl?query=YTA7&submit=Search", "YTA7")	=HYPERLINK("http://db.yeastgenome.org/cgi-bin/search/quickSearch.pl?query=AGP1&submit=Search", "AGP1")	=HYPERLINK("http://db.yeastgenome.org/cgi-bin/search/quickSearch.pl?query=YER130C&submit=Search", "YER130C")	=HYPERLINK("http://db.yeastgenome.org/cgi-bin/search/quickSearch.pl?query=GDH2&submit=Search", "GDH2")	
 							General transcriptional co-repressor, acts together with Tup1p; also acts as part of a transcriptional co-activator complex that recruits the SWI/SNF and SAGA complexes to promoters	Multifunctional enzyme of the peroxisomal fatty acid beta-oxidation pathway; has 3-hydroxyacyl-CoA dehydrogenase and enoyl-CoA hydratase activities	Transaldolase of unknown function; transcription is repressed by Mot1p and induced by alpha-factor and during diauxic shift; null mutant non-quiescent cells exhibit reduced reproductive capacity	Inositol 1-phosphate synthase, involved in synthesis of inositol phosphates and inositol-containing phospholipids; transcription is coregulated with other phospholipid biosynthetic genes by Ino2p and Ino4p, which bind the UASINO DNA element	Cytoplasmic protein containing a zinc finger domain with sequence similarity to that of Type I J-proteins; computational analysis of large-scale protein-protein interaction data suggests a possible role in actin patch assembly	Zinc cluster transcriptional activator necessary for derepression of a variety of genes under non-fermentative growth conditions, active after diauxic shift, binds carbon source responsive elements	None	Serine/threonine protein kinase involved in sphingolipid-mediated signaling pathway that controls endocytosis; activates Ypk1p and Ykr2p, components of signaling cascade required for maintenance of cell wall integrity; redundant with Pkh1p	Nonessential putative protein kinase of unknown cellular role; member of the LAMMER family of protein kinases, which are serine/threonine kinases also capable of phosphorylating tyrosine residues	Nuclear protein proposed to regulate utilization of nonfermentable carbon sources and endocytosis of plasma membrane proteins; overproduction suppresses chs5 spa2 lethality at high temp; ubiquitinated by Rsp5p, deubiquitinated by Ubp2p	Ubiquitin, becomes conjugated to proteins, marking them for selective degradation via the ubiquitin-26S proteasome system; essential for the cellular stress response; encoded as a polyubiquitin precursor comprised of 5 head-to-tail repeats	None	Putative S-adenosylmethionine-dependent methyltransferase of the seven beta-strand family, required for accurate meiotic chromosome segregation; null mutant displays increased levels of spontaneous Rad52 foci	Protein that acts with Mms22p in a repair pathway that may be involved in resolving replication intermediates or preventing the damage caused by blocked replication forks; implicated in regulation of Ty1 transposition	None	Protein kinase of the bud neck involved in the septin checkpoint, associates with septin proteins, negatively regulates Swe1p by phosphorylation, shows structural homology to bud neck kinases Gin4p and Hsl1p	Mitochondrial peroxiredoxin (1-Cys Prx) with thioredoxin peroxidase activity, has a role in reduction of hydroperoxides; induced during respiratory growth and under conditions of oxidative stress; phosphorylated	Putative FAD transporter; required for uptake of FAD into endoplasmic reticulum; involved in cell wall maintenance	Cytoplasmic chaperone of the Hsp90 family, redundant in function and nearly identical with Hsp82p, and together they are essential; expressed constitutively at 10-fold higher basal levels than HSP82 and induced 2-3 fold by heat shock	Multistress response protein, expression is activated by a variety of xenobiotic agents and environmental or physiological stresses	Transcriptional coactivator, facilitates elongation by influencing enzymes that modify RNAP II, acts in a peroxide resistance pathway involving Rad2p; suppressor of TFIIB mutations	Mitochondrial succinate-fumarate transporter, transports succinate into and fumarate out of the mitochondrion; required for ethanol and acetate utilization	Catalytic subunit of the SWI/SNF chromatin remodeling complex involved in transcriptional regulation; contains DNA-stimulated ATPase activity; functions interdependently in transcriptional activation with Snf5p and Snf6p	Protein of unknown function that may interact with ribosomes, based on co-purification experiments; homolog of human BAP31 protein	Protein involved in negative regulation of transcription of iron regulon; forms an iron independent complex with Fra2p, Grx3p, and Grx4p; cytosolic; mutant fails to repress transcription of iron regulon and is defective in spore formation	Protein that localizes to chromatin and has a role in regulation of histone gene expression; has a bromodomain-like region that interacts with the N-terminal tail of histone H3, and an ATPase domain; potentially phosphorylated by Cdc28p	Low-affinity amino acid permease with broad substrate range, involved in uptake of asparagine, glutamine, and other amino acids; expression is regulated by the SPS plasma membrane amino acid sensor system (Ssy1p-Ptr3p-Ssy5p)	None	NAD(+)-dependent glutamate dehydrogenase, degrades glutamate to ammonia and alpha-ketoglutarate; expression sensitive to nitrogen catabolite repression and intracellular ammonia levels	
